http_fetch_tls.pem is a self-signed TEST certificate and private key for the name fetch.test,
used only by tests/test_http_fetch.py (the TLS cases). It is not a secret and is trusted by
nothing except those tests, which load it as their own CA. It is committed because the standard
library cannot generate certificates and the test dependencies include no library that can.

Regenerate (valid 100 years, key and certificate concatenated):

  openssl req -x509 -newkey ec -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:prime256v1 -nodes -days 36500 \
    -subj /CN=fetch.test -addext subjectAltName=DNS:fetch.test \
    -addext basicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE -keyout key.pem -out cert.pem
  cat key.pem cert.pem > http_fetch_tls.pem
